1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,583
Transition metals are superb catalysts, for two reasons.

2
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:07,421
First, variable oxidation states.

3
00:00:07,421 --> 00:00:14,127
Persulphate and iodide are both negative ions, so they repel and react slowly.

4
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:16,276
Add iron three plus.

5
00:00:16,276 --> 00:00:21,666
It oxidises iodide to iodine, becoming iron two plus.

6
00:00:21,666 --> 00:00:26,197
Then persulphate oxidises it back to iron three plus.

7
00:00:26,197 --> 00:00:29,648
The iron goes round and round, and is not used up.

